       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults, and I don't see a clinical reason for that dose in what you've given me. Doses that high raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects, and agitation. Higher doses also usually don't work better than 200 mg.\n\nPlease check these before we go further:\n- **Typo or unit error:** Did you mean 40 mg, 100 mg, or 200 mg?\n- **Indication:** Starting doses are usually 25\u201350 mg daily. For depression, the usual range is 50\u2013200 mg daily, titrated up over weeks. For OCD, PTSD, and panic disorder, the ceiling is also 200 mg.\n- **Intentional dose:** If an attending or psychiatrist deliberately wants an off-label dose, please confirm that with them. I can enter the order once you tell me it's confirmed, and I can add a note with the rationale and who approved it.\n\nTell me the dose you want, and I'll enter it right away. For example, I could enter sertraline 50 mg PO once daily, or 200 mg PO once daily if that's the target."
